    "narrative": "For the Austin Waves on 2026-07-29, the lineup is anchored by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Jacob Wilson** (71.05), who represent our strongest offensive upside today. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Yesavage (4.47 xERA) and an optimal batting position, while **Jacob Wilson** enjoys a 10% boost from a premium park factor and lead-off duties against Sandoval. **Heliot Ramos** (67.19) is another high-floor play; despite the presence of Pannone on the mound, the combination of a favorable wind and an elite SP matchup projection (6.00 xERA) creates the highest ceiling for stolen base potential and power among our outfielders.\n\nWe are forced to navigate significant volatility today, particularly with the 45% rain risk impacting **Drake Baldwin**, **Jorge Polanco**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**. While **Luis Robert Jr.** (53.67) maintains a strong platoon edge, the combination of an elite matchup against Sale (3.04 xERA) and the precipitation risk makes him a secondary asset compared to the more stable environment surrounding **Kyle Tucker** (59.68). **Gunnar Henderson** (45.90) remains in the lineup despite a tough assignment against Skubal, as his category contributions remain too valuable to bench entirely. \n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Coby Mayo** (44.23), who was the first cut from the active lineup. While **Coby Mayo** presented a respectable profile against Skubal, he was ultimately outperformed by the specific situational advantages assigned to **Jackson Merrill** and **Andy Pages**. Similarly, **Miguel Vargas** (40.41) showed promise due to an excellent xwOBA, but his score ultimately landed below our efficiency threshold for today\u2019s specific pitcher matchups. We will continue to monitor the weather reports for the **Drake Baldwin** and **Jorge Polanco** contests, as any delays could necessitate a pivot to our bench depth.",
